From 31a1842b1d26caf6558a6f7e1aeed64b5430fc3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] SEQ MIDI OUT: the tracks' mutes as CC 103; a silent
 track sends no note-on

Vizz 1.0's mute and solo report (patches 0003, 0004 on Skiff 1.4) on
2.0's one MUTE. A track is silent as its sound is, the evaluation of
perform.c perf_begin / perf_mute: its MUTE (P_MUTE: a black key tapped
in GLO, FX or PERFORM, the MIXER), or, unless perf_kill turns the
layers' effects off, the MUTE held (2.0: cut only while held; FX's
perf_held, GLO's and PERFORM's perf_cut) or GLO's SOLO held on another
track (perf_solo; 2.0 keeps SOLO). A silent track sends no note-on; its
note-offs and its step CC 102 go on. Turning silent with notes sent
sounding: CC 123 on its channel first.

CC 103 on the track's channel (T1..T6 CHANNEL) says it: 127 silent,
0 sounding. Sent when it changes (compared every audio block with what
was sent last: keys, holds, solo, launches, loads, a channel change; a
channel changed with notes sounding: CC 123 on the old one), for all
six right after Start, on every bar while playing (16 1/16 steps,
either clock), when SEQ MIDI OUT turns ON and when USB comes up.
Nothing while SEQ MIDI OUT is OFF.

tests/seqmidi_test.c: cases 1-8 of docs/FIRMWARE-MUTE.md, the held
MUTE in GLO, FX and PERFORM (127 while held, then 0, the MUTE as it
was), FX's tap. ui_test, perform_test: the CC 103 owed after USB comes
up go out before the keys' MIDI is counted; smk_ui_test: the TRS
jack's clock counted by its bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Z5NrMFizGcfqt3zdrJXAX
